From 2b4d9aa8cf968df052822966507c3d62a9674229 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 19:32:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] AI_AB_TEST Economy 0052: a city-state declaration counts for
 the bans only if the war stands

The user: "a civ that never fights stays banned from wonders and gifts all game. an
aggressive civ that doesn't fight is a failed state anyway."

bullygreedy23 16DAE4CC (ab-0cb5402): the Aztecs "declared" on Singapore every turn from T48
to T71. CP's city-state peace undid each one (War fixed that in 5fe900a1), but each one set
HasStrikeDeclared. After the strike's OVER at T106 (the core obsolete), the bans
(IsStrikeNoWonders after OVER) saw a civ that had declared. They lifted: the Artists' and
Writers' Guilds, the Statue of Zeus, Notre Dame, and city-state gold to Ur and Mogadishu,
with no war fought all game.

Now SetStrikeDeclared(eTarget):
- On a major, it counts at once (CP doesn't undo those).
- On a city-state, it is pending (m_iStrikeDeclared = 2 + the city-state) and is confirmed
  at the next UpdateStrikeState only if we are still at war with it; otherwise it is
  cleared. Both outcomes are logged.
HasStrikeDeclared means confirmed only. Every ban chokepoint (canConstruct, the gift and
saving gates, buyout and marriage, the diplomacy loop, the production gates, the Great
Engineer) reads it through IsStrikeNoWonders.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G2NZj2nf4FeZTEHWjvnhhA
